1
00:00:00,235 --> 00:00:05,153
An order for zero items just went
through. Before we change the code,

2
00:00:05,383 --> 00:00:07,717
what should the validator do with
zero?

3
00:00:09,673 --> 00:00:14,826
Hold that answer. Open the test file
and find the case for a single item.

4
00:00:16,028 --> 00:00:19,125
Copy that test. Change the quantity to
zero,

5
00:00:19,476 --> 00:00:21,730
and change the expected result to
false.

6
00:00:23,174 --> 00:00:27,166
Now run just that test. See the two
values on the screen?

7
00:00:29,092 --> 00:00:34,091
We expected false. We got true. That
red line gives us a case

8
00:00:34,091 --> 00:00:35,127
we can reproduce.

9
00:00:36,548 --> 00:00:40,331
Replace greater than or equal to zero
with greater than zero.

10
00:00:40,863 --> 00:00:42,398
Run the same test again.

11
00:00:43,550 --> 00:00:47,424
This time it passes. Before we call
the fix complete,

12
00:00:47,835 --> 00:00:50,288
which neighboring value would you
check next?
